.TH "NOTIFICATION.NAVIGATE" "3JS" "October 9, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Notification.navigate \- Notification: navigate property
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]navigate\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]Notification\f[R] interface contains the URL the user agent will
navigate to when the user activates the notification.
.PP
This is the resolved value of the URL, if any, that was specified in the
\f[CR]navigate\f[R] option of the \f[CR]Notification()\f[R] constructor
or \f[CR]ServiceWorkerRegistration.showNotification()\f[R].
.PP
Normally, activating a non\-persistent notification fires the
\f[CR]click\f[R] event on its \f[CR]Notification\f[R] object, and
activating a persistent notification fires the
\f[CR]notificationclick\f[R] event on the
\f[CR]ServiceWorkerGlobalScope\f[R].
.PP
When a notification with a navigation URL is activated by the user, the
user agent navigates to the specified URL instead of firing either of
these events.
This allows notifications to direct users to a specific page without
requiring an event handler.
.SH VALUE
A string containing a URL, or an empty string if no navigation URL has
been set.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Reading the navigate property value
The \f[CR]navigate\f[R] property returns the resolved URL string when a
navigation URL has been set, or an empty string otherwise.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] notification = \f[B]new\f[R] Notification(\(dqNew message from Alice\(dq, {
  body: \(dqHey, are you free for lunch?\(dq,
  navigate: \(dq/messages/alice\(dq,
});

\f[I]// The property contains the resolved absolute URL\f[R]
console.log(notification.navigate); \f[I]// e.g. \(dqhttps://example.com/messages/alice\(dq\f[R]

\f[I]// Without a navigate option, the property is an empty string\f[R]
\f[B]const\f[R] basic = \f[B]new\f[R] Notification(\(dqHello!\(dq);
console.log(basic.navigate); \f[I]// \(dq\(dq\f[R]
.EE
.SS Using navigate with a service worker
When using persistent notifications through a service worker, the
\f[CR]navigate\f[R] option allows the notification to open a page when
activated, without needing to handle the \f[CR]notificationclick\f[R]
event.
.IP
.EX
\f[I]// Inside a service worker\f[R]
self.registration.showNotification(\(dqOrder shipped!\(dq, {
  body: \(dqYour order #1234 has been shipped.\(dq,
  navigate: \(dq/orders/1234\(dq,
});
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
Using the Notifications API
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]Notification()\f[R] constructor
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]ServiceWorkerRegistration.showNotification()\f[R]
